From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:40:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bypass TileLang wrapper caches when caching is disabled

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Local-base: b26f48b85790b832993f2c9d240dc3c39d6075e8, the five-patch refresh from deployment PR #875.
Upstream-source: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3710
Upstream-head: 99c2cd99f7b3510b40365e3d9fac2afba576a46e

Rationale: A cache-disabled compilation must bypass the JIT wrapper caches as well as the persistent cache, so fresh compilation checks cannot silently reuse an earlier kernel.

Quality: Retain the local prepare/freeze API and named errors. Normal cache-enabled serving behavior is retained; disabled-cache requests intentionally compile afresh.

Tests: Five cache tests and the default prepare/freeze compatibility check pass in two fresh processes each.
Recorded compiler tree: 1fe7e7955686439282edb5579d3805f093ee69bf.
See this candidate's results.json and immutable raw receipts. Full image,
retained-feature and serving qualification remain separate gates.

Upstream-status: open PR, checked 2026-11-04; pinned experimental backport.
Remove this local backport when advancing to an upstream revision containing it.
